# The tokens copy only what is printed (copiable values, CR 707.2), not whether the original is tapped (ruling 2025-07-25).
# Bot1's Llanowar Elves attacks on turn 3 and is tapped in the second main phase; Devastating Onslaught for X=1 (three mana
# from the Moxen) then makes an Elves token that enters UNTAPPED while the original stays tapped. The token is sacrificed
# at the end step and the original stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Llanowar Elves
Devastating Onslaught
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Llanowar Elves > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Devastating Onslaught.Cast(Llanowar Elves; X: 1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves#1.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves#2.Token = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves#2.Tapped = false
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Emerald; Mox Ruby; Mox Jet; Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 4
Bot1.Graveyard = Devastating Onslaught
